  × This mutates state inside the written computed property.
  
     6 │     // Vue 2 exports `set` as a named function as well as hanging it off `Vue`.
     7 │     written() {
   > 8 │       return set(this, 'foo', 'lorem')
       │              ^^^
     9 │     },
    10 │   },
  
  i A computed value is cached and recomputed only when a dependency changes, so the getter does not run a predictable number of times — and neither does this mutation.
  
  i Derive the value instead of mutating: copy before reordering, with slice() or toReversed(). If the write is the point, move it to a watcher, a method, or the computed property's own setter.
  
